Hash Tables map a key to a value.
we use them in spell checkers (can look up a word amongst thousands of words immediately)
we use them in dictionaries to find meaning of a word,
we use them on compilers (compiler use them to find address of a variable or functions)
we use them on code editor
....


we call Hash Tables:
HashMap in JAVA
Object in JAVA Script
Dictionary in Python

HashTable has 3 functionalities, and all of them are O(1)
INSERT  O(1)
LOOKUP  O(1)
DELETE  O(1)

NOTE: if we have very bad designed
      and we have so much collisions,
      our functionalities could be O(n) on hash tables.
      but in standard design and good load factor
      it is O(1)
